  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math></p><p>have infinitely many solutions. Then the system</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;has :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "oeGaU",
      "text": "infinitely many solutions",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
